# Spider-Byte's "up to one target" (CR 601.2c, 115.1): two targets are refused; Bot1 chooses no target on turn 3, so nothing returns to a hand - Bot1's Ornithopter
# and Bot2's Memnite both stay on the battlefield.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Ornithopter
Spider-Byte, Web Warden
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Spider-Byte, Web Warden.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter; Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite)
Bot1.Target()
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Ornithopter; Spider-Byte, Web Warden
Bot2.Battlefield = Memnite
